sequenceDiagram
    participant UI as Settings Screen
    participant Pop as Popup Window
    participant B as Connections Service
    participant C as CLI Process (claude / openai)
    participant P as Provider (Anthropic / OpenAI)

    UI->>B: GET /api/connections/anthropic/oauth-start
    B->>B: resolve CLI binary (env var → PATH → well-known paths)

    alt CLI binary not found
        B-->>UI: 200 { available: false }
        UI->>UI: hide "Login with browser"; show API key input only
    end

    B->>C: spawn: claude login --print-login-url  (non-blocking)
    C-->>B: auth URL (first stdout line)
    B->>B: store { pid, state_token, started_at } in _cli_login_pending[conn_id]
    B-->>UI: 200 { available: true, flow: "cli_browser", url, poll_url: ".../cli-login-status" }

    UI->>Pop: window.open(url, 600×700 popup)
    Note over Pop,P: user completes auth in provider's browser tab
    P->>C: auth completion signal
    C->>C: write credentials to ~/.claude/ or ~/.config/openai/

    loop every 2 s (max 5 min)
        UI->>B: GET /api/connections/anthropic/cli-login-status
        B->>C: claude whoami (probe)
        alt whoami exits non-zero
            C-->>B: error
            B-->>UI: { status: "pending" }
        else whoami exits 0
            C-->>B: 0 + username
            B->>B: status → connected; clear _cli_login_pending entry
            B-->>UI: { status: "connected", username: "acisse@…" }
            UI->>Pop: popup.close()  (if still open)
            UI->>B: GET /api/connections
            B-->>UI: updated list; Anthropic card → connected
        else TTL exceeded (5 min)
            B-->>UI: { status: "error", error_message: "Login timed out" }
            UI->>UI: show error; offer retry
        end
    end